      "content": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <memory>\n#include <vector>\n\nclass FastScanner {\n    static constexpr int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    int idx = 0;\n    int size = 0;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\npublic:\n    inline char getChar() {\n        if (idx >= size) {\n            size = (int)fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n            idx = 0;\n            if (size == 0) return '\\0';\n        }\n        return buf[idx++];\n    }\n\n    int nextInt() {\n        char c;\n        do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\n        int sign = 1;\n        if (c == '-') {\n            sign = -1;\n            c = getChar();\n        }\n        int x = 0;\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n            c = getChar();\n        }\n        return sign * x;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    const size_t ringSize = (size_t)s + 1;\n    std::unique_ptr<int[]> ring(new int[ringSize * (size_t)n]);\n    std::vector<long long> col(n, 0);\n\n    for (int r = 0; r < s; ++r) {\n        int* row = &ring[(size_t)r * n];\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4) {\n            int v0 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v1 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v2 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v3 = fs.nextInt();\n            row[j] = v0;\n            row[j+1] = v1;\n            row[j+2] = v2;\n            row[j+3] = v3;\n            col[j] += v0;\n            col[j+1] += v1;\n            col[j+2] += v2;\n            col[j+3] += v3;\n        }\n        for (; j < n; ++j) {\n            int v = fs.nextInt();\n            row[j] = v;\n            col[j] += v;\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long cur = 0;\n    for (int j = 0; j < s; ++j) cur += col[j];\n    long long best = cur;\n\n    int limit = n - s;\n    for (int j = 1; j <= limit; ++j) {\n        cur += col[j + s - 1] - col[j - 1];\n        if (cur > best) best = cur;\n    }\n\n    size_t outSlot = 0;\n    size_t inSlot = ((size_t)s) % ringSize;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= limit; ++i) {\n        int* pout = &ring[outSlot * (size_t)n];\n        int* pin = &ring[inSlot * (size_t)n];\n\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4) {\n            int v0 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v1 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v2 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v3 = fs.nextInt();\n            pin[j] = v0;\n            pin[j+1] = v1;\n            pin[j+2] = v2;\n            pin[j+3] = v3;\n            col[j] += (long long)v0 - pout[j];\n            col[j+1] += (long long)v1 - pout[j+1];\n            col[j+2] += (long long)v2 - pout[j+2];\n            col[j+3] += (long long)v3 - pout[j+3];\n        }\n        for (; j < n; ++j) {\n            int v = fs.nextInt();\n            pin[j] = v;\n            col[j] += (long long)v - pout[j];\n        }\n\n        cur = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < s; ++j) cur += col[j];\n        if (cur > best) best = cur;\n\n        for (int j = 1; j <= limit; ++j) {\n            cur += col[j + s - 1] - col[j - 1];\n            if (cur > best) best = cur;\n        }\n\n        if (++outSlot == ringSize) outSlot = 0;\n        if (++inSlot == ringSize) inSlot = 0;\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", (long long)best);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replacing modulo-based ring indexing with increment-and-wrap rolling counters and unrolling the column-sum update loop by four reduces per-iteration arithmetic overhead, improves instruction-level parallelism, and keeps memory accesses streaming sequentially through the flat ring buffer and column array on ARM64.",
  "notes": "Only src/solution.cpp was modified. The algorithm remains O(N^2) with a (S+1)-row ring; correctness is preserved for all valid inputs because rolling indices reproduce exactly the same slot sequence as modulo arithmetic, and unrolled loops handle tails explicitly.",
